@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title The four harness paradigms — intended working mode per def

component "claudecode\n**ML blackbox algorithm**\nspec → plan → implement → verify → loop" as CC <<app>>
component "cursor\n**Policy-gated blackbox**\nsame autonomous loop, bounded by\nnative deny rules + root-owned hooks" as CU <<app>>
component "opencode\n**Subagent crew**\nsoftware team with HITL oversight" as OC <<app>>
component "cecli\n**Pair-programming sniper**\nprecise, low-token, human-guided" as CE <<app>>

note bottom of CC
  Steering: ""CLAUDE.md""
  Posture: ""--dangerously-skip-permissions"" (intentional —
  made acceptable by the egress boundary, not by
  in-container restraint)
  Detail: _spec/defs/claudecode/claudecode-paradigm.puml
end note

note bottom of CU
  Steering: "".cursor/rules/*.mdc"", ""cli-config.json"", ""hooks.json""
  Posture: ""--force"", but deny rules and enterprise hooks
  still win — the boundary is layered, not bypassed
  Detail: _spec/defs/cursor/cursor-paradigm.puml
end note

note bottom of OC
  Steering: ""AGENTS.md"" + seeded subagents
  Posture: role-based; reviewers read-only
  Detail: _spec/defs/opencode/opencode-paradigm.puml
end note

note bottom of CE
  Steering: ""CONVENTIONS.md"" + "".cecli.conf.yml""
  Posture: conservative; no blanket dangerous flag
  Detail: _spec/defs/cecli/cecli-paradigm.puml
end note

note top of CC
  **Why paradigms are specified at all.** Entrypoints,
  seeded configs and steering files are optimized per
  harness. A change to any def must preserve its paradigm
  — otherwise the defaults drift into a fifth, unstated
  mode that no diagram describes.

  What they **share** is the containment model, not the
  permission posture: same runtime-user boundary, same
  git-identity flow, same egress + credential boundary.
end note

' --- IGNORE: layout hints (do not edit) ---
CC -right[hidden]- CU
OC -right[hidden]- CE
CC -down[hidden]- OC
' --- END IGNORE ---
@enduml
